## Meta Ads — CPA, last week (2026-10-24 → 2026-10-30)

**Headline:** CPA came in at **$190.00**, down from **$197.99** the prior week (2026-10-17 → 2026-10-23) — a change of **-$7.99 (-4.0%)**.

**Absolute figures (source: ad platform):**

| Metric | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $3,761.84 | $3,039.99 | -$721.85 (-19.2%) |
| Conversions | 19 | 16 | -3 (-15.8%) |
| CPA | $197.99 | $190.00 | -$7.99 (-4.0%) |

**Likely driver:** Spend was cut harder (-19.2%) than conversions fell (-15.8%), so efficiency improved slightly despite lower volume. This looks like a "spend-down, results-down roughly in line" week rather than a genuine efficiency gain — I don't have campaign-level breakdown from these tools to confirm where the spend reduction happened.

**Caveats:**
- Data is complete through 2026-10-30, so both windows are full weeks.
- Conversion volume is small (16 vs. 19) — a 3-conversion swing makes the CPA change noisy; a single conversion either way would move CPA by roughly ±$10–12. Treat the -4.0% as effectively flat within uncertainty.
- No campaign/ad-set detail available here, so the driver attribution is directional, not verified.

